{"ticker":"AGARWALEYE","symbol":"AGARWALEYE","instrumentId":3193974,"name":"Dr. Agarwals Health","industry":"NSE-Medical-Hospitals","about":"Dr Agarwal’s Eye Hospitals provide specialized eye care across 13 states and 3 Union Territories in India, including Tamil Nadu, Karnataka, Maharashtra, and Gujarat. Their Chennai flagship center is a global leader in eye care, research, and academic training. Internationally, the hospital network extends across 9 African countries, including Ghana, Uganda, Kenya, and Mauritius. They offer world-class treatments for conditions such as cataracts, glaucoma, diabetic retinopathy, retinal detachment, and pediatric ophthalmology. Advanced procedures like vitrectomy, photocoagulation, PDEK, and refractive surgery ensure comprehensive eye care. Their expertise spans retina, uvea, cornea, and orbit-related conditions, delivering excellence in ophthalmology worldwide.","website":"www.dragarwals.co.in","location":null,"exchange":"NSE","fetchedAt":"2026-11-20T13:16:43.825Z","basis":"consolidated","price":{"value":549.5,"changePct":1.7686822853967874,"week52High":560.7,"week52Low":406.55},"stats":[{"label":"Market capitalization","value":"₹17,425 Cr"},{"label":"Sales","value":"₹2,363 Cr"},{"label":"Shares in float","value":"215,627,000"},{"label":"No. of funds","value":"103"},{"label":"Shares held by funds","value":"207,430,272"},{"label":"Dividend yield","value":"0.00%"},{"label":"Book value","value":"8.6"},{"label":"U/D vol ratio","value":"1.6"},{"label":"LTDebt / equity","value":"7.0%"},{"label":"Alpha","value":"0.05"},{"label":"Beta","value":"0.31"},{"label":"EPS growth rate","value":"32%"},{"label":"P/E ratio","value":"101.76"},{"label":"5-year P/E range","value":"100–158"},{"label":"Return on equity","value":"6.6%"},{"label":"Cash flow (INR)","value":"16.38"},{"label":"Volume","value":"81,826"},{"label":"Avg volume (50d)","value":"244,272"},{"label":"Master score","value":"69"},{"label":"EPS rating","value":"88"},{"label":"Price stre